          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong retrofunctor
            (sometimes called a
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong cofunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of a retrofunctor goes in the
            %em opposite
            direction to the assignment on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
          %p
            Retrofunctors generalise both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijective+on+objects+functor"} bijective-on-objects functors
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibrations"} discrete opfibrations
          %p
            Retrofunctors arise naturally in the study
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+a+monoidal+category"} non-cartesian internal categories
          %p
            In the literature, the terminology “cofunctor” is common. However, terminology is misleading, as a cofunctor is not the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite"} opposite
            of a functor. Moreover, the terminology “cofunctor” is also used for a morphism of
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                cocategories
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cocategories"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+retromorphism"} monad retromorphism
            (of which retrofunctors are a motivating example).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong retrofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↛
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi : A \nrightarrow B
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists of a map sending each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            to an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi φ
                    %mn 0
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_{0}a \in B
            and a map sending each pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi φ
                    %mn 0
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a \in A, u : \varphi_{0}a \to b \in B)
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi φ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_{1}(a, u) : a \to a'
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_{1}
                respects codomains:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi φ
                        %mn 0
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mi cod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi_{0}a' = cod(u)
                where
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi cod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi φ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
